reading: if eye-movement-only decoding matches overt decoding, and a model trained
on eye movements transfers to overt trials, the overt left/right signal is at
least partly oculomotor. Covert attention (eyes fixed) is the test of attention
proper: above-chance covert decoding, and no transfer from eye movements to covert
trials, would mean a left/right attention signal that is not the eye movement.
